+- **Reset route.** A selected edge with a manual route shows a **Reset route** button (the outline button style, 32 px, 44 px for a coarse pointer) above its label, reachable with Tab after the handles. It removes the manual route in an undo step of its own and returns focus to the edge. The toolbar then stays where it was clicked, and the same **Reset route** button stays in its slot, dimmed, `aria-disabled` and titled "The connection already routes automatically." (#207). Without that, the toolbar would re-centre on the automatic route's label with **Reset route** gone, and the second press of a double click, landing on the point of the first, would hit **Remove connection**. Keeping the toolbar where it was is not enough alone, nor is keeping the button in its slot: each still leaves **Remove connection** under the point. A **Crosses a card** note that was showing stays as a blank of its width, hidden from assistive technology. The held button keeps its hit target, focus and `nopan`; its click, Enter and Space do nothing, and its click ends on the button as **Remove connection**'s does, so Control or Meta cannot select the connection again and toggle it off. **Remove connection** stays where it was and works as usual. The hold is `RouteHandles`' own state: no timer, no click-count guard, no event suppression and no change to the route editing interface, the shared gesture gate or the selection. It ends when the toolbar unmounts (the connection is deselected, or a load, a refused stale action or a removal drops the selection), or when a manual route is drawn again after the automatic one: an Undo, a nudge or a drag, whichever array the route arrives as. Fresh selection of an automatic route shows **Remove connection** alone, centred on its label. While held, the toolbar may sit apart from the automatic label or from a card moved since, and it can cover a handle or the label; nothing releases it on a pan or a card drag. A press just outside the button, in the 8 px gap, reaches whatever is under the toolbar, never **Remove connection**.
 - **Look.** Handles are 12 px dots in the selected-edge stroke (`--canvas-edge-selected`, 3:1 on `--canvas-bg`, an existing registered pair) on the raised surface, filled on hover, with a 24 px target (44 px under a coarse pointer); keyboard focus draws the `--focus-ring` ring (3:1 on the canvas). They are scaled against the zoom, so they keep their screen size. Forced colours use `Canvas`, `CanvasText`, and `Highlight`; the toolbar takes system colours. Styles live in `styles/canvas-routes.css`.
 - **Tests.** `editor/manual-route.test.ts` (the stored form, segments, moves and splits, normalisation, nudges, smoothstep equivalence), `editor/routing-manual.test.ts` (fixed routes in the plan, node moves, crossing and fallback, reservations, incremental equality and the replanning bound), `editor/OrthogonalEdge.test.tsx`, `editor/Canvas.test.tsx` (drag, nudge, reset, crossing, node moves, undo), `editor/store.test.ts`, `editor/useRouting.test.ts`, contracts and domain round-trips, the engine test above, and Edge E2E in `e2e/edge-routes.spec.ts`. The QA hand-off with screenshots is [docs/qa/2026-10-05-issue-44-waypoints](qa/2026-10-05-issue-44-waypoints/README.md).
 
